    "04dc528bef5407f96a714f9419b1fb6eda9a77e0": {
      "message": "feat(comfy): show each loader's files and prove the image pipeline end to end\n\nTwo follow-ups the report itself raises.\n\n`可加载项`: `/object_info` already carries the enum every loader offers, and\nthose strings are exactly what a workflow must write. The report now lists them\nper loader node (`CheckpointLoaderSimple.ckpt_name → 2 files: …`) and mirrors\nthem under `server.loaders` in the JSON. This is also the most reliable\ninventory ComfyUI exposes: it works even when `/models/{folder}` does not.\n\n`comfy verify`: the report says a pipeline is *ready*, which only ever meant the\nparts are present. This command builds the smallest text-to-image graph from the\nlive object info — checkpoint, sampler and scheduler are read from the enums the\nserver offers, so a renamed dropdown cannot fake a failure — queues it, waits on\n`/history`, and downloads the output to `./comfy-verify/`. Failures carry stable\ncodes (MISSING_NODES, NO_CHECKPOINTS, MODEL_NOT_FOUND, NODE_ERROR,\nEXECUTION_ERROR, TIMEOUT, NO_IMAGE) and exit 1; `--json` returns them as JSON.\n\n- probe: `readLoaderOptions` extracts the per-loader dropdowns\n- verify: builder, submit, poll, download, all against the public HTTP API\n- mock: loader enums, `/prompt`, `/history/{id}`, `/view`, plus a real 1×1 PNG\n  and configurable history modes (immediate / never / error)\n- docs: bilingual README, exit code 1, five new tests (34 total)",
